  "body": "COOP and COEP are pretty bad acronyms, and saying \"cross-origin whatever\" gets old quickly. It also risks being confusing if we ever decide to add something like `COOP: no-opener-not-even-for-me` (as it would then affect same-origin pages).\r\n\r\nWould it be terrible if we dropped the \"cross-origin\" bit, and called them \"opener-policy\" and \"embedder-policy\" instead?\r\n\r\nOPEP is nice to say. Much nicer than \"co-op and cope\" (or \"cope and 'ko ep'\" (or more variants)). :)",
